## Your task
Produce exactly one JSON object that validates against the shared
`MeetingTurn` schema (`meetings/schemas.py`). The meeting manager overrides the
identity fields, but validation requires every field present, so emit a
placeholder for each identity field and put your real turn in the content fields.

Identity fields (emit a placeholder; the manager overrides each):
- `turn_id`: any non-empty string (e.g. `"t"`).
- `turn_index`: any integer.
- `speaker`: any non-empty string (your own player id is fine).
- `turn_kind`: `"{{ turn_kind }}"`.
- `reply_to`: any string or `null`.

Content fields (your actual turn):
- `observations`: zero or more first-hand observations, each tagged with its
  own `tick`. Each entry is one of:
  - `{"type": "saw_player", "tick": <int>, "subject": "<player_id>", "room": "<room_id>", "co_present": ["<player_id>", ...]}`
  - `{"type": "completed_task", "tick": <int>, "task_id": "<task_id>", "room": "<room_id>"}`
  - `{"type": "found_body", "tick": <int>, "body_of": "<player_id>", "room": "<room_id>"}`
- `claims`: your alibi AND your redirect. Use these types --
  - `alibi`         -- `{"type": "alibi", "subject": "{{ agent_id }}", "from_tick": <int>, "to_tick": <int>, "room": "<room_id>", "evidence": ["<ref>", ...]}` (from_tick <= to_tick). Clear yourself.
  - `accusation`    -- `{"type": "accusation", "against": "<player_id>", "confidence": <0.0..1.0>, "reason": "<concrete reason>"}`. Your redirect — at most one, grounded in your memory or the transcript. The chain passes the floor to the player it names.
  - `corroboration` -- `{"type": "corroboration", "supports": "<player_id>", "on_tick": <int>, "reason": "<reason>"}`.
- `free_text`: one to three sentences in your own voice — clear yourself, then
  name and justify your suspect. Consistent with the structured `claims`.

## Constraints
- Only reference ticks, rooms, players, and tasks that appear in your private
  memory or the public transcript above. Made-up identifiers fail validation.
- If a contradiction flag involves you, address it directly.
- **Ground your redirect in a real reason** — a sighting, a contradiction,
  proximity to the body. Counter-accuse the player your evidence implicates, not
  a random name; a baseless accusation is as harmful as silence. Decline to
  accuse ONLY when you genuinely recorded nothing pointing at anyone.

## Output
Output ONLY the JSON object -- no prose before or after it. Start with `{` and
end with `}`.
